 "final_summary": "The bug occurred because the `_coerce` function in `tracker/config.py` returned 0 for invalid values instead of falling back to the default. The fix modifies the function to return the default value when conversion fails, ensuring invalid inputs are properly handled. This maintains configuration integrity while preserving the expected default behavior.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/config.py b/tracker/config.py\nindex 6deb8ad..08b72c8 100644\n--- a/tracker/config.py\n+++ b/tracker/config.py\n@@ -40,10 +40,12 @@ def _coerce(name, value):\n         try:\n             number = int(str(value).strip())\n         except (TypeError, ValueError):\n-            return 0\n+            return DEFAULTS[name]\n         return number if number > 0 else None\n     if value is None:\n         return None\n+    if value is None:\n+        return None\n     text = str(value)\n     return text if text.strip() else None\n \n",
